    "body": "_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: stacked on #439 (base is its branch `claude/citar-key-italic`); merge #439 first.\n- Depends on: #439. Both edit `sp-citations--layout-templates` (this one adds `%lastfirst` to the author field of the `main` template; #439 builds the `completion` template from it).\n- If merged first (before #439): the diff shows #439's change too, and merging it lands both; nothing breaks, but #439 is no longer separately reviewable.\n- After merging #439: retarget this PR to `main` (GitHub does it when the base branch is deleted on merge); no other conflicts expected with the DEVONthink stack (#415, #418-#421) or #426.\n\n## Summary\n\n- The author column now shows the last name first, then the first names: `Smith, John; Doe, Jane`. New `sp-citations--last-first`, the `lastfirst` transform of `citar-display-transform-functions`, used as `${author editor:N%lastfirst}` in the `main` template.\n- BibTeX names are `Last, First` or `First Last`, whichever way they were typed, and citar showed them raw. Now:\n  - `Last, First` stays; `Jane Q. Doe` becomes `Doe, Jane Q.`.\n  - Particles stay with the last name (`Ludwig van Beethoven` becomes `van Beethoven, Ludwig`); so does a suffix (`Martin Luther King Jr.` becomes `King Jr., Martin Luther`; `Smith, Jr., John` becomes `Smith Jr., John`).\n  - Names in braces (organisations) and single words are left as they are; `others` becomes `et al.`\n  - Several names are joined with `; ` (a comma would clash with the one inside each name). Editors are shown the same way when there is no author.\n- The value is cut to the column width like any other, and the cut part stays hidden in the candidate, so searching still finds every author. The `preview` template is unchanged. The citekey styling from #439 is untouched.\n- Limits: the particle list is a fixed set of common ones (von, van, de, der, di, la, le, …); a particle typed with a capital is taken as part of the first names. LaTeX accents are not converted.\n- Tests: `tests/sp-citations-layout-test.el`, 13 pass (17 name cases, nil, the template uses the transform, plus the earlier ones). Tangle check passes.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists). No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) (untested by Claude: GUI, real bibliography)\n- [ ] `C-c w b o` (`citar-open`): the author column reads `Last, First` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] An entry with several authors shows `Smith, John; Doe, Jane`\n- [ ] An entry whose BibTeX author is typed `First Last` shows `Last, First`\n- [ ] An entry with a `van`/`de` name, one with `Jr.`, one with an organisation in braces, and an editor-only book look right\n- [ ] Search for a second or third author's last name: the entry is still found\n- [ ] The citekey is still faded and italic; the columns still line up\n- [ ] Regression: `citar-insert-citation` and `citar-create-note` work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to the previous branch in the stack, `git -C ~/dotfiles switch claude/citar-key-italic`, or to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/citar-author-last-first` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- No notes or vault files change, so nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
